      "writtenOn": "2026-02-08T14:38:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m still not sure why DRLR would be necessary to the ExpandFromResolve, and this a bit similar to Shahbaz\u0027s question/surprise about input attachment working here. What this CL seem to try to do is to sample the resolve attachment to write it to the MSAA render target, before any of the FS run on the same pixel.\n\nIt seem like we don\u0027t need all the input attachment magic, and instead could have the resolve target in `VK_IMAGE_LAYOUT_GENERAL`, and run `PerformExpandResolveDraw` with normal texture sampling (of the resolve target) (not input attachments), and .. that\u0027s it? No need for DRLR nor barriers, nor input attachments.",
      "parentUuid": "ef1abbe8_1595e73f",
      "revId": "abbcbf94a1d3e9ee8c789632f83b931a13d37c1e",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
