      "lineNbr": 374,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002296
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-02-18T06:18:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So I raised this with the WG https://gitlab.khronos.org/vulkan/vulkan/-/issues/4687 and got confirmation that, although this usage of DRLR was not thought of, it\u0027s _supposed_ to work.\n\nI ended up writing tests for it here: https://gerrit.khronos.org/c/vk-gl-cts/+/19613, which fails on RADV due to some depth/stencil related driver bug I believe, but does pass for color.\n\nTL;DR, the algorithm is fine, but if the new tests expose a driver bug about it, you\u0027d need to disable the path for those older drivers.",
      "parentUuid": "62216d24_5849e69a",
      "revId": "abbcbf94a1d3e9ee8c789632f83b931a13d37c1e",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a63e5771_f0a5a2f5",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/vulkan/ResolveTextureLoadingUtilsVk.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 374,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002296
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-03-25T15:00:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "After much back and forth, the WG decision was that this is illegal. DRLR simply never intended to allow input attachments to map to resolve attachments, and my test is never going to work on some hardware.",
      "parentUuid": "54b7bb2b_b61dec00",
      "revId": "abbcbf94a1d3e9ee8c789632f83b931a13d37c1e",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "967b2585_21e6fcb2",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/vulkan/ResolveTextureLoadingUtilsVk.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 374,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002296
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-03-25T16:06:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That said, you _can_ make this work by actually splitting the render pass in 2, and using \"read-only input attachments\" that are not mapped to any render pass attachments in the first pass to do the unresolve. That split has no perf difference on IMRs, and on TBRs you can rely on VK_EXT_msrtss. But in that case, using a texture instead of input attachment also works like Corentin was suggesting (i.e. you don\u0027t need DRLR).\n\n_However_, if the user (Skia) can use MSAA images and _not_ invalidate them, avoiding the need to ever unresolve because MSAA data is still there, then on IMRs it should be even faster to avoid doing any of this. The unresolve pass is costly on IMRs, and it\u0027ll be better to not expose this functionality.\n\nThe only reason I see why you\u0027d want to expose it on IMRs is if for example Skia does some rendering single-sampled, then wants to blend something multisampled over it, and this gives a convenience function... but again, Skia could have done a texture-based unresolve in that case itself.",
      "parentUuid": "a63e5771_f0a5a2f5",
      "revId": "abbcbf94a1d3e9ee8c789632f83b931a13d37c1e",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8c052a80_0e2fad55",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/vulkan/ResolveTextureLoadingUtilsVk.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 374,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003501
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-03-25T16:22:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e However, if the user (Skia) can use MSAA images and not invalidate them, avoiding the need to ever unresolve because MSAA data is still there, then on IMRs it should be even faster to avoid doing any of this\n\nUsing MSAA without unresolves might be faster on IMRs. However, unresolves are still useful for Skia to reuse MSAA texture between render passes. In order to reuse, we have to treat the MSAA texture as a scratch texture. It can also allows using a MSAA texture smaller than the resolve texture itself. It can massively save memory usage, (at least observed on Windows). Without this, the memory usage of Graphite is much more than Ganesh.\n\nThat\u0027s said. I think we can skip exposing this feature on IMRs. Without it, Skia will emulate the unresolves using separate render passes already. It\u0027s similar to the approach you mentioned.",
      "parentUuid": "967b2585_21e6fcb2",
      "revId": "abbcbf94a1d3e9ee8c789632f83b931a13d37c1e",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
