        "id": 1002296
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-02-08T17:23:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Assuming a future framebuffer functionality will come, there are three pairs that might need synchronization:\n\n* Expand writes to color, real render pass also writes to color. With legacy render pass objects, I see I added a `VkSubpassDependency2` for it in ANGLE but that was because there were two subpasses involved. You\u0027re probably right that you won\u0027t need such a thing here (assuming this usage is correct, which I still doubt because otherwise why couldn\u0027t we do that with legacy RPs in one pass too?).\n* Expand reads from resolve attachment, real render pass writes to resolve attachment. This is a WaR hazard that only needs an execution barrier: FS -\u003e COLOR_ATTACHMENT\n* For framebuffer fetch functionality, Expand writes to color, real render pass reads from color. If `VK_EXT_rasterization_order_attachment_access` is not supported, you\u0027d need a COLOR_ATTACHMENT/WRITE -\u003e FS/READ barrier (which is the one that is written here currently!)",
      "parentUuid": "2b6f39a9_42c20fe4",
      "revId": "abbcbf94a1d3e9ee8c789632f83b931a13d37c1e",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
